\name{TrialDesignPlanQuantitativeBayes}
\alias{TrialDesignPlanQuantitativeBayes}
\title{Bayesian Quantitative Trial Decision Rule}
\description{
Internal Bayesian decision-rule class. Obtain instances through
\code{\link[=getDesignQuantitative]{getDesignQuantitative()}} with bayesian = TRUE or explicit criteria.
}
\details{
Inherits optional reference values and percentiles from
TrialDesignPlanQuantitativeBase. These are NA for freely specified criteria.
Go, Stop and Indeterminate 1 must be provably mutually exclusive for every
continuous posterior CDF; Indeterminate 2 includes all remaining outcomes,
including exact probability-threshold ties. Priors are supplied to the OC
functions, rather than stored in the decision rule.
}
\section{Inherited fields}{

\describe{\item{\code{targetValue}}{Optional target effect on the beneficial-effect scale. A supplied finite scalar for reference-value rules; NA for explicit Bayesian criteria.}
\item{\code{lowerReferenceValue}}{Optional lower reference effect on the beneficial-effect scale. A supplied finite scalar for reference-value rules; NA for explicit Bayesian criteria.}
\item{\code{upperPercentile}}{Upper percentile supplied for a reference-value rule, strictly between lowerPercentile and 1. NA for explicit Bayesian criteria. For Bayesian rules its interpretation is controlled by percentileMapping.}
\item{\code{lowerPercentile}}{Lower percentile supplied for a reference-value rule, strictly between 0 and upperPercentile. NA for explicit Bayesian criteria. For Bayesian rules its interpretation is controlled by percentileMapping.}}
}

